  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2003-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The slope of \\(f\\) is \\[ \\frac{f(6) - f(2)}{6 - 2} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3. \\]\n\nTherefore \\[ f(12) - f(2) = 3(12 - 2) = 30. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "A linear function has a constant rate of change (slope)",
        "The slope is \\(\\dfrac{f(6) - f(2)}{6 - 2},\\) and the answer is that slope times \\(12 - 2\\)"
      ],
